      "difficulty_reason": "The authors convert smooth Boolean-function distributions with large uniform empirical deviation into average-case smooth codes by symmetrization, then use a fat-shattering/VC construction to recover true locally decodable codes. The reverse direction builds smooth low-degree decoding polynomials. Both complete conversions and the corrected final-version proof of the distribution-to-average-code theorem are retained as one characterization.",
